---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import StudyNav from "../../components/studies/StudyNav.astro";
import StudyBanner from "../../components/studies/StudyBanner.astro";
import Chip from "../../components/studies/Chip.astro";
import { assumptions, plans } from "../../data/studies";
import { trinityRelease } from "../../data/trinity";
const A = assumptions.assumptions as { id: string; value: string; status: string; use: string; source?: string; url?: string; observed?: string }[];
---

<Base
  title="Method, sources & assumptions — Ivan Minier"
  theme="studies"
  description="How the Trinity Residential Design Studies are made: the assumption register, sources, AI use, checks, and the written-feedback revision workflow."
>
  <header class="st-hero wrap-wide">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Studies · Method</p>
      <h1>Method, sources & assumptions</h1>
      <p class="lede">How the drawings and models are made, what they rely on, and how to change them.</p>
    </div>
    <StudyBanner />
  </header>
  <StudyNav />

  <section class="wrap-wide st-section">
    <span class="st-num">How the drawings are made</span>
    <div class="st-cols">
      <div class="st-prose">
        <h2>Drawings from data, not pictures.</h2>
        <p>
          Each plan is a small, editable data file: rooms as rectangles in feet, doors on shared
          walls, windows on exterior walls, and furniture and fixtures. A generator draws walls,
          door swings, windows, labels, dimensions, and a title block, and exports SVG, PNG, PDF,
          DXF (for CAD, in feet), and a room schedule.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before anything is drawn, a checker tests the geometry: rooms that overlap, doors that do
          not sit on a shared wall, rooms with no access, windows on interior walls, furniture
          outside its room or overlapping, door swings that hit furniture, and bed counts that do
          not match. It caught three real conflicts while the first drafts were made.
        </p>
        <p>
          Floors are assembled from suites by reference, so changing a suite updates every floor
          that uses it. Whole-building test fits and the development model read their numbers from
          the generated schedules, and Trinity figures come from the proposal's own data
          (Version {trinityRelease.version}).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="st-card">
        <h3>Who did what</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Ivan Minier:</strong> the Trinity program and goals (Peaks and Rise), design intent, the choice of University Heights as a reference, the source floor plans supplied for benchmarking, and review of every output.</li>
          <li><strong>AI assistance (Claude):</strong> drafting layouts and options, writing the generator, checks, test-fit and finance arithmetic, and first drafts of page text. AI suggestions are listed separately in each plan's design notes.</li>
          <li><strong>No professional</strong> architect, engineer, planner, or cost consultant has reviewed this work.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap-wide st-section">
    <span class="st-num">Revising a plan</span>
    <h2>Change the drawings by writing what you want.</h2>
    <ol class="st-prose">
      <li>Describe the change in plain words — "make the six-person lounge two feet deeper", "swap Rise Option A's flex room for a third bathroom", "replace suites N7 and N8 with an accessible suite".</li>
      <li>The current version is frozen into the plan's history before anything changes.</li>
      <li>The plan's data file is edited and its version number raised; new dimensions are added to the assumption register.</li>
      <li>All drawings, schedules, floors that use the plan, test fits, and model inputs are regenerated and re-checked; any error stops the build.</li>
      <li>The change is logged with whose instruction it was (mine or an AI suggestion), and the before/after beds and areas.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="caption">Current plans: {plans.map((p) => `${p.id} v${p.version}`).join(" · ")}. Full instructions ship with the source files (studies/README.md).</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap-wide st-section">
    <span class="st-num">Assumption register</span>
    <h2>Every dimension, and where it came from.</h2>
    <div class="st-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Assumption register">
      <table class="st-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Id</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Used for / source</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {A.map((a) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{a.id}</td>
              <td>{a.value}</td>
              <td><Chip k={a.status} /></td>
              <td>{a.use}{a.source && <><br /><small>{a.url ? <a href={a.url}>{a.source}</a> : a.source}{a.observed && ` · observed ${a.observed}`}</small></>}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
        <caption>Updated {assumptions.updated}. "Exploratory" values have no measured basis and must be replaced by measured or professionally reviewed values before any reliance. "Reference" values were read from UVM floor plans supplied by the author; those drawings are not published here.</caption>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap-wide st-section">
    <span class="st-num">Sources</span>
    <h2>Sources used in the studies.</h2>
    <ul class="st-prose">
      <li>Trinity Redistricting, Version {trinityRelease.version} ({trinityRelease.dateLabel}) — figures, zoning summary, benchmarks, and source ledger: <a href="https://trinityredistricting.com/methods.html">trinityredistricting.com/methods.html</a></li>
      <li>UVM Housing & Dining, University Heights North and South (room types, bathroom and kitchen arrangement), observed 6 Nov 2026: <a href="https://www.uvm.edu/housingdining/university-heights-north-and-south">uvm.edu</a></li>
      <li>UVM Housing & Dining, Costs (AY 2026-27 and 2027-28 room rates), observed 6 Nov 2026: <a href="https://www.uvm.edu/housingdining/costs">uvm.edu/housingdining/costs</a></li>
      <li>UVM Housing & Dining, Fall 2026 move-in guide (mattress size and provided furniture), observed 6 Nov 2026: <a href="https://www.uvm.edu/housingdining/move-guide-fall-2026">uvm.edu</a></li>
      <li>University Heights North + South floor plans (UVM), supplied by the author for reference; room areas only, not reproduced.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
